{
    "$schema": "../schema/registry-item.schema.json",
    "name": "auth-ui-react",
    "title": "Auth UI — React",
    "description": "Copy-in, user-owned React auth screens on top of the base `auth` item and @lunora/react: sign in/up, forgot/reset password, magic link, email OTP, two-factor (verify + setup), account & security settings, and organizations. Framework-agnostic controllers under lunora/auth-ui/core, thin React views under lunora/auth-ui/react, and minimal token-aligned CSS — no Tailwind. Edit anything; upgrades are 3-way merged.",
    "docs": "Import the stylesheet once and wrap your auth routes in <AuthUIProvider>: `import { AuthUIProvider, SignInCard } from './lunora/auth-ui/react'; import { authClient } from './lunora/auth-ui/client'; import './lunora/auth-ui/styles.css';`. Pass your router into `nav` (and optionally `Link`) so navigation uses client-side transitions — e.g. react-router `{ navigate, replace }` from useNavigate. Enable optional flows by also running `lunora add auth-magic-link` / `auth-otp` (server halves) and flipping the matching `plugins` in lunora/auth-ui/client.ts. Requires the base `auth` server item (auto-added). Social buttons render for the providers you pass as `social={['github', ...]}`, or for whichever ones the server discloses when you pass none; either way the provider must be configured server-side. Mounting <AuthView> on a nested route (`/auth/:view`) also needs `viewPaths={{ base: '/auth' }}`, which is what the links between the screens and the two-factor redirect are derived from.",
    "requires": ["auth"],
    "deps": { "@lunora/auth": "workspace:*", "@lunora/errors": "workspace:*", "@lunora/react": "workspace:*", "better-auth": "1.7.1" },
